\description{
Fit one linear model per feature of a feature-by-sample table and test each named coefficient, and each contrast of a contrasts file with its confidence interval, with limma's empirical-Bayes moderated t, Benjamini-Hochberg adjusted, in one call.

Runs mzLib's \code{LinearModel.Fit} once - every design column is fitted - and then
\code{EmpiricalBayes.Moderate} for each coefficient you name, which also applies Benjamini-Hochberg
across that coefficient's fitted features. This is limma's \code{lmFit()} then
\code{eBayes(legacy = TRUE)} (Smyth 2004), which mzLib holds to limma to 1e-8 relative on limma's own
reference output. With \code{contrasts}, \code{EmpiricalBayes.ModerateContrasts} also tests each row of a
contrasts file - "250 ng against 125 ng", "the mean of two groups against a third" - with its
confidence interval: limma's \code{contrasts.fit()} then \code{eBayes()} then \code{topTable(confint = ...)}.
}
\details{
A feature is fitted on the samples where it was observed, and is reported - never dropped - when
it cannot be: \code{"too_few_observations"} when it has no more observed samples than the design has
coefficients, \code{"rank_deficient"} when its observed samples cannot separate the coefficients (a
feature seen in only one group cannot have a group effect).
}
